\b CVScan PRD — Job Inbox and Australian Job Search Expansion\b0\par
\par
\b 1. Product summary\b0\par
CVScan already helps users improve resumes, generate cover letters, scan job descriptions, and track applications. This next scope sharpens the product around one practical promise: find jobs from anywhere, understand whether they are worth applying to, tailor fast, and keep the whole search organized.\par
\par
\b 2. Why this matters\b0\par
Job seekers in Australia often search across multiple sources, save screenshots, copy links, and lose track of where they found roles. The current market has job boards, trackers, and resume tools, but most users still stitch the workflow together manually. CVScan can win by becoming the workflow layer over the top of that fragmented process.\par
\par
\b 3. Product goals\b0\par
- Improve activation after signup\par
- Increase saved jobs and tracker usage\par
- Make resume upload and first job action feel immediate\par
- Build the foundation for the strongest candidate-side search flow in Australia\par
\par
\b 4. Target users\b0\par
- New graduates\par
- Career switchers\par
- International and visa candidates\par
- Active job hunters managing many tabs and sources\par
\par
\b 5. Core user promise\b0\par
Paste a job link or upload a screenshot, and CVScan will extract the role, tell you if it is worth applying to, save it to your tracker, and help you tailor your application.\par
\par
\b 6. Scope\b0\par
Six small wins:\par
1. Resume-to-job-match instant suggestions\par
2. Paste job URL import\par
3. Screenshot-to-job parser\par
4. Apply / Stretch / Skip verdict\par
5. Multi-source save into one tracker\par
6. Duplicate job merging\par
\par
Three-step job search layer:\par
- Step 1: Universal Job Inbox\par
- Step 2: Light Aggregation Layer\par
- Step 3: Unified CVScan Search Layer\par
\par
\b 7. Success metrics\b0\par
- Faster time to first saved job\par
- More jobs saved per active user\par
- Higher tracker revisit rate\par
- More resume tailoring actions after job import\par
- Better week 1 and week 4 retention for users who use the Job Inbox\par
\par
\b 8. Guardrails\b0\par
CVScan should not depend on unauthorized scraping of restricted platforms. It should win through user-assisted capture, normalized tracking, decision support, and legally safer aggregation sources.\par
\par
\b 9. Source of truth\b0\par
For implementation planning and agent execution, docs/Build_Spec.md and later docs/Build_Spec* files are the source of truth.\par
